    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah, i was thinking the same. i actually ran a quick rough model on it and it looks like the static schedule might drop sequestration efficiency by maybe 8-10% in the high-fluctuation periods. but the cloud savings are just so massive that the board might not care about a small drop in intake. do you think that 10% dip is something we can actually live with, or is it gonna break our year-end targets?",
